# Reproducer 1: Untyped Container Indexing
# Category: Insufficiently documented static-polymorphism rules / specialization defect
# Command: moss check repro_untyped_index.moss --json
#
# Observed behavior:
# Fails with MOSS_COMPILE_ERROR: "value is not an indexable container" at line 3.
# Even though Moss supports duck typing for method calls on untyped parameters,
# container indexing (items[i]) is rejected before specialization if the parameter
# is untyped.

fn get_first(items):
  return items[0]

fn main():
  echo get_first([10, 20])
